  "term": "epigenetic landscape",
  "definition": "Epigenetic landscape refers to the overall pattern of epigenetic changes affecting gene regulation in cells, such as DNA methylation and histone modifications. In this context, it describes shifts in those marks that are linked to changes in gene expression and cellular function.",
